# wgime.bat MUST stay pure CRLF / no BOM: cmd.exe relies on CRLF to parse the
# batch header (labels / parenthesized blocks / exit /b). A pure-LF checkout makes
# cmd fall through into the PowerShell body with "'xxx' is not recognized" errors
# and the IME never starts. PowerShell / C# handle CRLF fine.
# Stored as-is (CRLF in the blob): `-text` disables git's line-ending conversion
# (with core.autocrlf=true, `text eol=crlf` would corrupt the CRLF pairs).
wgime.bat -text
wgtray.bat -text
